Step 1 — Update Your System
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

Step 2 — Download Wazuh Installer
curl -sO https://packages.wazuh.com/4.7.5/wazuh-install.sh

Step 3 — Install Wazuh (All-in-One)
* This installs:
** Wazuh Manager
** Wazuh Indexer
** Wazuh Dashboard
*sudo bash wazuh-install.sh -a

Step 4 — Get Login Credentials
After installation, credentials are saved in a file.
sudo tar -O -xvf wazuh-install-files.tar wazuh-install-files/wazuh-passwords.txt
admin: <password>

Step 5 — Check Services
Make sure everything is running:

* sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager
* sudo systemctl status wazuh-indexer
* sudo systemctl status wazuh-dashboard

You want:
active (running)
Also check on what port the indexer is listening
New installs often use port 443 (NOT 5601)

Step 6 — Open Wazuh Dashboard
* From your browser:
** https://<your-server-ip>

** Bypass HTTPS Warning
** You’ll see:
“Your connection is not private”
* Click:
** Advanced
** Proceed

Step 7 — Login
Username: admin
Password: (from Step 4)

Step 8 — Verify It Works
Inside dashboard:
Go to Security Events
Search:
event.id: *

Step 9 — Install Wazuh Agent (on Windows)
On your Windows VM:
Download agent from Wazuh website

* Install it
** During setup:
Install & Configure Wazuh Agent on Windows 11
Download Wazuh agent for Windows: Wazuh Downloads
Install agent with default options. During setup, specify Manager IP (192.168.xx.xxx) and port 1514, 1515 and 56000 (TCP/UDP).

After installation, edit ossec.conf if needed:

<server>
  <address>192.168.xx.xxx</address>
</server>
Start the agent service:
net start WazuhAgent

** Enter Wazuh server IP

* Register agent manually (if needed)

* On Windows:
** "C:\Program Files (x86)\ossec-agent\agent-auth.exe" -m <WAZUH-SERVER-IP>
* Then start agent:
** net start wazuh-agent

Step 10 — Confirm Agent Connected

On server:
sudo /var/ossec/bin/agent_control -l
You should see your Windows machine listed.

Step 12 — Start Seeing Logs
In dashboard:

Go to Endpoints → Agents
Click your Windows agent
Go to Events

Common Issues (Quick Fixes)
** Can’t access dashboard

Try:
https://<ip>

Check:
sudo ss -tulnp | grep 443

** Dashboard shows errors

Check:
sudo systemctl status wazuh-indexer

** No logs from Windows

Restart agent:
net stop wazuh-agent
net start wazuh-agent
